-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 20261104.2~sparky9~0 (2026-11-04)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Plain-HTTP apt sources are refused for now (ORDER 400; CVE-2026-109518, DSA-6607-1; Daniel, 2026-11-04: "change them to https", "block http sources for now"): /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/00sparky-block-plain-http, a conffile, sets Acquire::http::Proxy to http://plain-http-blocked-cve-2026-109518.invalid/ and Acquire::https::Proxy to DIRECT, so a plain http:// source fails with "Could not resolve 'plain-http-blocked-cve-2026-109518.invalid'". The same file the main session wrote by hand on the station and the A10
  * The postinst turns plain http:// into https:// in /etc/apt/sources.list and /etc/apt/sources.list.d/*.list and *.sources (lines that are not comments), copies every file it changes to /var/backups/sparky-stereo-apt/<UTC stamp>/<path> first, and prints each file and its copy. A source with no HTTPS fails at apt update with apt's own error
  * THE BLOCK IS TEMPORARY: it leaves in the first version after apt 3.3.6 is in Debian testing (that version removes the file, rm_conffile). The conversion to https stays
  * sparky-stereo.sources, with deb-src, is now the one place of the edition's source index: sparky-stereo-ffmpeg-fdk 20261104.1 removes its own sparky-stereo-ffmpeg-src.sources (the duplicate that made apt say "Target Sources ... is configured multiple times") and depends on this version. No image builds this package with DEB_SRC=0 (build.sh's default is 1; only refresh-final-metadata.py sets it, to 1)
  * sparky-stereo-only-ours, sparky-stereo and the icon setting are unchanged from 20261104.1~sparky9~0

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 20261104.1~sparky9~0 (2026-11-04)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * The edition's carried NVIDIA 580 user space is no candidate without a driver lock (ORDER 390): a record in sparky-stereo for the source packages the locks name (nvidia-graphics-drivers, nvidia-open, nvidia-modprobe, nvidia-persistenced, nvidia-settings, nvidia-xconfig, libnvidia-nscq, libnvsdm, nvidia-fabricmanager, nvidia-imex, cuda-drivers*), from the edition's repository only, at -1. The locks' own files sort first and raise them (1005 for the 580 set under the legacy lock), so a stack chosen by Hardware Setup is unchanged; this record applies on a system with neither lock
  * Why: on a system with no lock, the first apt dist-upgrade after installing the round replaced Debian's nvidia-detect 550.163.01-5.1 with our nvidia-kernel-support 580.196.07-1+sparky2+lc1 (which Provides, Conflicts and Replaces nvidia-detect) and installed nvidia-modprobe 580 and NVIDIA's modprobe, udev and alternate-install files, though no NVIDIA stack was chosen; Hardware Setup runs /usr/bin/nvidia-detect, which our package does not have. apt 3.3's solver calls a package obsolete when another binary of its source has a higher source version at an equal or higher priority (apt-pkg/depsolver.cc, ObsoletedByNewerSourceVersion), and the edition's 580 (1001) was above Debian's 550 (500). Measured in clean containers: 3 NVIDIA changes before, 0 after; a person's own Debian nvidia-modprobe 610 was also moved to our 580 by that dist-upgrade (1 change before, 0 after)
  * sparky-stereo-only-ours is unchanged from 20261103.1~sparky9~0; rerun make-only-ours.py over the round's cohort at publication (the packages of ORDER 391 and 331 are not in it)

